682	    // terminal fd (SIGTTIN). When bivvy is not the terminal's foreground
683	    // process group (e.g., `cargo run`), this triggers suspension.
684	    //
685	    // The SIGTTOU signal is ignored in main.rs, but these tests verify:
686	    //   1. The prompt code doesn't panic or crash on non-TTY
687	    //   2. Yes/no and multi-option selects produce consistent error behavior
688	    //
689	    // History: These tests were originally added in commit 09d5292, then
690	    // removed in commit 520c90c when the custom yes/no prompt was
691	    // reintroduced. Removing them allowed the SIGTTOU regression to go
692	    // undetected. They are restored here to prevent that from happening
693	    // again.
694	    //
695	    // If you need to change prompt_yes_no's output formatting, do so
696	    // WITHOUT removing these tests. The custom yes/no prompt (y/n
697	    // shortcuts, cursor guard, styled indicators) is a legitimate
698	    // customization — but it MUST coexist with SIGTTOU safety.
